[2.347849, "o", "\u001b[?25h\r\n"]
[2.347957, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L5 · THE WIRE BACK — your terminal, still waiting \u001b[2m─────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.450017, "o", "│  SSE stream open. heartbeats keep every timeout alive. client: spinner,\r\n"]
[2.450117, "o", "│  no read timeout set. server: batch slot held. billing: per token.\r\n│  \u001b[2mnothing is broken anywhere. that's the terrifying part.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[2.450149, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L6 · THE ORCHESTRATOR — the loop lives where meaning lives \u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│  vLLM-style server · CUDA graphs · continuous batching\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.550487, "o", "│  the loop isn't a for-statement a human wrote — it's a scheduler calling\r\n"]
[2.550697, "o", "│  generate() forever because nothing defines 'done'. \u001b[31mthe only layer\r\n│  where 'meaning' still exists — the only layer where the loop can be broken.\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│  watchdog inventory: client 0 · gateway 0 · scheduler 0 · sampler 0\u001b[0m\r\n│  in field sessions, the only layer that ever stops the loop is the human:\r\n"]
[2.550854, "o", "│  \u001b[33mCtrl+C, 4/4. the human layer outperformed every automated layer.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.550893, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L7 · CUDA KERNEL — the spiral, written in C \u001b[2m───────────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.656052, "o", "│  \u001b[36mgridDim [165] · blockDim [256]\u001b[0m · each thread: \u001b[33mfor (k=0; k<K; k+=16) accumulate(A×B)\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.656182, "o", "│  a nested for-loop: K-loop inside, grid outside. the K-loop exits. the\r\n│  outer one was never given an exit. \u001b[2m~40 launches/token, forever.\u001b[0m\r\n\r\n"]
[2.656211, "o", "\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L8 · TENSOR CORE — 2 billion ticks/second of pure obedience \u001b[2m───────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.656229, "o", "\u001b[2m│  132 SMs · HMMA.m16n8k16 = 4,096 FLOP/issue\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[2.756547, "o", "│  one token = 3,906,250 MMAs. pure math ~15µs; real decode \u001b[31m4.8 ms\u001b[0m — bandwidth-bound, not compute-bound.\r\n"]
