[10.35903, "o", "\r\n\u001b[1m\u001b[36m┌─ L20 · THE PLANCK WALL — where the word 'deeper' breaks \u001b[2m────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[2m│  planck length 1.6×10⁻³⁵ m · planck time 5.4×10⁻⁴⁴ s\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.464077, "o", "│  resolving anything smaller needs so much energy in so small a volume that\r\n"]
[10.464149, "o", "│  it collapses into a black hole. \u001b[31mwith known physics, resolution fails —\r\n"]
[10.46419, "o", "│  'smaller' stops being answerable.\u001b[0m not a proven limit of nature — the limit\r\n"]
[10.464205, "o", "│  of the math we currently have. \u001b[33mthe wall is a boundary of theory, not a\r\n│  measured wall of the universe.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
[10.464214, "o", "│  one GPU clock tick spans ~10³⁴ planck ticks. \u001b[33meternity is granular.\u001b[0m\r\n"]
